# !! DO NOT TYPE A REAL VALUE INTO THIS FILE. It is committed and this repository is
# !! PUBLIC. The placeholder is deliberately not blank, so a value left unreplaced fails
# !! loudly at tinkerbell's 401 instead of silently becoming an empty credential.
#
# TEMPLATE, committed. The real secret is .env.secret.mcp-gateway-tinkerbell.encrypted, and
# that ciphertext is the only copy. It was committed holding this placeholder; write the real
# value with, from the repo root:
#
#   ./scripts/onepassword-secrets.mts edit apps/production/browser-chaperone/.env.secret.mcp-gateway-tinkerbell
#
# Run it YOURSELF rather than asking the agent to, for the reason
# env.secret.mcp-gateway-google.example gives. The value is a NEW tinkerbell API token
# (`tb_api_...`) minted for the gateway, not the one olya-0 held as TINKERBELL_API_TOKEN:
# that one was readable from her pod, so it is revoked in tinkerbell once this is deployed
# (activescott/browser-chaperone#44, docs/mcp-gateway.md "Tinkerbell").
tinkerbell_api_token=<REPLACE-ME-with-a-tinkerbell-api-token>
